    Refine messaging Premium rule (initiate vs reply) + fix a real recursion bug + video upload cap UI
    
    Business rule refinement: only the FIRST message in a conversation must
    come from a premium sender - replies are open to anyone, so a free player
    can respond to a conversation a premium scout already opened. Migration
    032 implements this; migration 033 fixes a real bug FOUND VIA TESTING in
    032's own policy - an infinite recursion error (the policy's subquery read
    from messages while evaluating a messages policy, re-triggering itself).
    Would have broken every message send, first or reply, if deployed as-is.
    Fixed with a SECURITY DEFINER helper function, matching the pattern
    already used everywhere else in this project - retested all 3 scenarios
    directly against live data afterward: non-premium blocked from
    initiating, premium succeeds initiating, and critically, a genuinely
    non-premium player successfully replies once the conversation has one
    message. All test data cleaned up both times.
    
    Messages UI: added a compact inline upgrade prompt in the input area
    (not the full PremiumGuard card) shown only when the CURRENT user is
    non-premium AND the selected conversation has zero messages - mirrors the
    server-side rule exactly rather than a separate, potentially-inconsistent
    frontend check.
    
    Video uploads: explicitly NOT wrapped in PremiumGuard, per instruction.
    VideoUpload.tsx now shows the real upload form normally for free users
    under the 3-video cap (matching the RLS policy from migration 031,
    unchanged), and only swaps to an upgrade prompt once the limit is
    reached - the upload UI works exactly as it always has until that point.
    
    All files syntax-checked.
